# Shell scripts run on Linux (NAS/VM) — must never get CRLF line endings
# from a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf), or bash chokes on \r (shebang,
# heredocs, comparisons all break in ways that are easy to miss on Windows
# since `bash -n` here doesn't catch a bad line-ending, only a real Linux
# bash does).
*.sh text eol=lf
